Optional tokenizer dependency notices

The tokenizer package imports github.com/hupe1980/go-tiktoken v0.0.9.
Its distribution includes the cl100k_base vocabulary in resource/cl100k_base.tiktoken
and a root MIT LICENSE, with no separate vocabulary license notice. The resource
is not copied into this SDK. Its 100,256 mergeable ranks match the resource used
by the official tiktoken implementation:
https://openaipublic.blob.core.windows.net/encodings/cl100k_base.tiktoken
SHA-256: 223921b76ee99bde995b7ff738513eef100fb51d18c93597a113bcffe865b2a7

Only applications importing this optional package link the vocabulary and regex
dependency. No vocabulary is downloaded at application startup. Ordinary Go
tests use committed vectors; regenerating them explicitly uses Python tiktoken
0.12.0 and may download its hash-verified reference vocabulary.

